  "description": "A generic atomic cell for .NET. Read, Write and Exchange allocate nothing, for any T. Lock-free for references and any unmanaged value up to a machine word, including the 3-, 5-, 6- and 7-byte structs that no interlocked instruction matches, and for Int64 and UInt64 on 32-bit runtimes too. Everything else takes a monitor instead, and Atomic<T>.IsLockFree reports which one you got. Ships a Roslyn analyzer that reports lock statements and Monitor calls on a cell.",
